                <pb facs="0782" n="684" sameAs="frus:frus1920v01/pg684"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/1457: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Harbin</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-09T17:00:00+08:26"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9, 1920—5
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 10—2:26
                    a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>General Horvat left to-day for Peking, announcement being he is on leave absence.
                    Pimenoff, manager of the Russo-Asiatic Bank will act as manager of the railway
                    during Horvat’s absence. Horvat will undoubtedly take up railway situation with
                    Peking authorities.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
